{
  "title": "16: al-Nahl النحل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَتٰۤى اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ فَلَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوْهُ‌ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(1)\nATAA AMRUL LAAHE FALAA TASTAA’JELOOHU WALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nThe Decree of God hath come, therefore ye hasten it not: Glory be to Him and Exalted is He above what they associate with Him.\nيُنَزِّلُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةَ بِالرُّوْحِ مِنْ اَمْرِهٖ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖۤ اَنْ اَنْذِرُوْۤا اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا فَاتَّقُوْنِ‏(2)\nYUNAZZELU AL-MALAAEKATA BEALRROOHE MIN AMREHI A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI AN AANZEROOA ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANAA FAT-TAQOON.\nHe sendeth down the angels with the spirit (revelation) by His own decree on whomsoever He willeth of His servants saying: “Warn ye (the mankind) that there is no god but I therefore fear Me.\nخَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ تَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(3)\nKHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQ TAA’AALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nCreated He the heavens and the earth with the truth; Exalted is He above what they associate (with Him).\nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ فَاِذَا هُوَ خَصِيْمٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(4)\nKHALAQAL INSAANA MIN NUTFATIN FA-EZAA HOWA KHASEEMUM MOBEEN.\nHe created man from life sperm or germ and behold! (that same drop now a man) he is an open disputer.\nوَالْاَنْعَامَ خَلَقَهَا‌ ۚ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا دِفْ ٴٌ وَّمَنَافِعُ وَمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(5)\nWAL AANA’AAMA KHALAQAHAA LAKUM FEEHAA DEF WA MANAA-FE-O’ WA MINHAA TAAKULOONA.\nAnd the cattle (He) created them for you, therein is warmth and many gains, and of them ye eat.\nوَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا جَمَالٌ حِيْنَ تُرِيْحُوْنَ وَحِيْنَ تَسْرَحُوْنَ‏(6)\nWA LAKUM FEEHAA JAMAALUN HEENA TUREEHOONA WA TASRAHOONA.\nAnd for you they beseem well when ye drive them (home) and when ye drive them forth (to pasture.)\nوَتَحْمِلُ اَثْقَالَكُمْ اِلٰى بَلَدٍ لَّمْ تَكُوْنُوْا بٰلِغِيْهِ اِلَّا بِشِقِّ الْاَنْفُسِ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكُمْ لَرَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌۙ‏(7)\nWA TAHMELO AASQAALAKUM ELAA BALADIN LAM TAKOONOO BAALEGHEEHE ILLAA BESHEQQE AL-AANFUSE INNAL TAQUL LA-RAOOFUR RAHEEM.\nAnd bear they your burdens to lands which ye could not else reach but with distress unto (your) self; Verily thy Lord is Pitiful, All-Merciful,\nوَّالْخَيْلَ وَالْبِغَالَ وَالْحَمِيْرَ لِتَرْكَبُوْهَا وَزِيْنَةً‌ ؕ وَيَخْلُقُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(8)\nWWAALKHAYLA WAL BEGHAALA WAL HAMEERA LETARKABOOHAA WAZEENATAN WA YAKHLOQO MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd (He made) horses and mules and asses that ye might ride upon them and as adornment; and createth He what ye know not.\nوَعَلَى اللّٰهِ قَصْدُ السَّبِيْلِ وَمِنْهَا جَآئِرٌ‌ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ لَهَدٰٮكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(9)\nWA LAAHE QASDU SABEELE WA MINHAA JAAERUN WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAHADAAKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nAnd upon God rests the guidance unto the right way, and of them (the ways) are the deviating ones; and if He willeth He would certainly guide you all aright.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً‌ لَّكُمْ مِّنْهُ شَرَابٌ وَّمِنْهُ شَجَرٌ فِيْهِ تُسِيْمُوْنَ‏(10)\nHOWA LAZEE ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN LAKUM MINHO SHARAABUN WWAMENHU SHAJARUN FEEHE TUSEEMOONA.\nHe it is Who sendeth down water from the heavens for you; from it ye drink, and by it (groweth) trees on which ye pasture your cattle.\nيُنْۢبِتُ لَكُمْ بِهِ الزَّرْعَ وَالزَّيْتُوْنَ وَالنَّخِيْلَ وَالْاَعْنَابَ وَمِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(11)\nYUNBETU LAKUM BEHIL AZ-ZARA’A WAALZZAYTOONA WAALNNAKHEELA WAL AAA’NAABA WA MIN KULLE AS-SAMARAATE INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nHe groweth for you thereby corn, and the olives, and the palm-trees, and the grapes, and of all the fruits; Verily in this is a sign for a people who reflect.\nوَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَۙ وَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ‌ؕ وَالنُّجُوْمُ مُسَخَّرٰتٌۢ بِاَمْرِهٖؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَۙ‏(12)\nSAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA WA SHAMSA WAL QAMARA WA NOJOOMUN MUSAKKHARAATUN BEAAMREH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd (He hath) made sub servient for you the night and the day and the sun and the moon; and the stars have been made subservient by His decree; Verily in this are signs for a people who understand,\nوَمَا ذَرَاَ لَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مُخْتَلِفًا اَلْوَانُهٗ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA MAA ZARAA LAKUM FIL ARZE MUKHTALEFAN AALWAANUH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YYAZZAKKAROONA.\nAnd what He hath produced in the earth of varied hues (and qualities) Verily there is in this a sign for a people who are mindful (with gratitude).\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ سَخَّرَ الْبَحْرَ لِتَاْكُلُوْا مِنْهُ لَحْمًا طَرِيًّا وَّتَسْتَخْرِجُوْا مِنْهُ حِلْيَةً تَلْبَسُوْنَهَا‌ۚ وَتَرَى الْفُلْكَ مَوَاخِرَ فِيْهِ وَلِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA HOWA LAZEE SAKKHARA BAHRA LE-TAAKOLOO MINHO SUMMA NAKSOOHAA TAREEA WWATASTAKHREJOOA MINHO HELYATAN TALBASOONAHAA WA TARAL AL-FULKA MAWAAKHERA FEEHE WA LETABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEHI WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nAnd He it is Who made subservient the sea that ye might eat from it fresh meat and take out from it ornaments which ye wear, and thou seest the ships cleaving through it, and that ye might seek of His grace, and that ye might give thanks.\nوَاَلْقٰى فِى الْاَرْضِ رَوَاسِىَ اَنْ تَمِيْدَ بِكُمْ وَاَنْهٰرًا وَّسُبُلًا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُوْنَۙ‏(15)\nWAALQAA FIL ARZE JA-A’LA AN TAMEEDA BEKUM WA KHELAALAHAA WWASUBULAN LA-A’LLAKUM TAHTADOON.\nAnd He hath cast great mountains (standing firm) in the earth lest it may shake with you, and rivers and the roads that ye be guided aright,\nوَعَلٰمٰتٍ‌ؕ وَبِالنَّجْمِ هُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(16)\nWAA’ALAAMAATIN WABEALNNAJME HUM YAHTADOON.\nAnd landmarks (too), and by the star they are guided (to the right way)\nاَفَمَنْ يَّخْلُقُ كَمَنْ لَّا يَخْلُقُ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(17)\nAFAMAWN YYAKHLUQU KAMAM LAA YAKHLUQU AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nWhat! Is He then who createth like unto him who createth not? Will ye not then consider?\nوَاِنْ تَعُدُّوْا نِعْمَةَ اللّٰهِ لَا تُحْصُوْهَاؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(18)\nWA TAU’UDDOOA NE’MATAL LAAHE LAA TUHSOOHAA INNAL LAAHA LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nIf ye would count God’s bounties, ye can not compute them; Verily God is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nوَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تُسِرُّوْنَ وَ مَا تُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(19)\nWAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MAA TUSERROONA WA MAA MAA TO’LENOON.\nAnd God knoweth what ye hide and what ye manifest\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَا يَخْلُقُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّهُمْ يُخْلَقُوْنَؕ‏(20)\nWAL LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAA YAKHLUQOONA SHAY-ANW WA HUM YUKHLAQOONA.\nAnd those whom they call on besides God create not aught while they are themselves created.\nاَمْوَاتٌ غَيْرُ اَحْيَآءٍ‌ ۚ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(21)\nAMWAAT GHAYRO AAHYAAIN WA MAA YASH-O’ROON AYYAANA YUB-A’SOON.\nDead (they are), not living, and they perceive not when they will be raised.\nاِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ‌‌ ۚ فَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ مُّنْكِرَةٌ وَّهُمْ مُّسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(22)\nELAAHOKUM ELAAHUN WAAHED FAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE QULOOBUHUM MMUNKERATUN WA HUM HUM MUSTAKBEROON.\nYour God is One God; and those who believe not in the hereafter, their hearts are repulsive (against the truth ), and they are men of pride.\nلَا جَرَمَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّوْنَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْتَكْبِرِيْنَ‏(23)\nLAA JARAMA ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA YOSIRROONA WA MAA YUA’LENOONA INNAHU LAA YOHIBBUL AL-MUSTAKBEREENA.\nCertainly it is that God knoweth what they hide and what they express; Verily He loveth not the proud ones.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ مَّاذَاۤ اَنْزَلَ رَبُّكُمْ‌ۙ قَالُوْۤا اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(24)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM MMAAZAA ANZALAL RABBOKUM QAALOO ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nAnd when it is said unto them: “What is it that your Lord hath sent down?” Say they (Nothing but the) legends of the ancients,\nلِيَحْمِلُوْۤا اَوْزَارَهُمْ كَامِلَةً يَّوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ۙ وَمِنْ اَوْزَارِ الَّذِيْنَ يُضِلُّوْنَهُمْ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ‌ؕ اَلَا سَآءَ مَا يَزِرُوْنَ‏(25)\nLEEHMELOOA AAWZAARAHUM KAAMELATAN YAWMA QEYAAMATE WA MIN AAWZAARE LAZEENA YUZELLOONAHUM BEGHAYRIL E’ELMIN ALAA SAAA-A MAA YAZEROONA.\nThat they may bear their burden entirely on the Day of Judgment and also of the burdens of those whom they led astray without knowledge; Behold! Evil is it what they bear!\nقَدْ مَكَرَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَاَتَى اللّٰهُ بُنْيَانَهُمْ مِّنَ الْقَوَاعِدِ فَخَرَّ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّقْفُ مِنْ فَوْقِهِمْ وَاَتٰٮهُمُ الْعَذَابُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(26)\nQAD MAKARA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FAATAA LAAHO BUNYAANAHUM MENAL AL-QAWAAE’EDE FAKHARRA A’LAYHEMUL AS-SAQFU MIN FAWQEHIM WAATAAHUMU A’ZAABO MIN HAYSO LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nIndeed did plot those before them, and then (the wrath of) God came (and destroyed) their structure (from) the foundations, and fell on them the roof from above them, and came on them the torment whence they perceived not.\nثُمَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ يُخْزِيْهِمْ وَيَقُوْلُ اَيْنَ شُرَكَآءِىَ الَّذِيْنَ كُنْتُمْ تُشَآقُّوْنَ فِيْهِمْ‌ؕ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ اِنَّ الْخِزْىَ الْيَوْمَ وَالسُّوْۤءَ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَۙ‏(27)\nSUMMA YAWMA QEYAAMATE YUKHZEEHEM WA YAQOOLO AYNA SHORAKAAA-EYAL LAZEENA KUNTUM TUSHAAQQOONA FEEHEM QAALA LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA INNAL AL-KHEZAAA YAWMA WAALSSOOA A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nThen on the Day of Resurrection He will bring them to disgrace and say: “Where are My partners (which ye ascribed unto Me), about whom ye have been disputing; Those who have been given the knowledge will say: “Verily the disgrace this day and evil is upon the infidels,\nالَّذِيْنَ تَتَوَفّٰٮهُمُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ ظَالِمِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ‌ فَاَلْقَوُا السَّلَمَ مَا كُنَّا نَعْمَلُ مِنْ سُوْۤءٍؕ بَلٰٓى اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(28)\nLAZEENA TATAWAFFAAHUMU AL-MALAAEKATU ZAALEMEAA ANFOSEHIM FAALQAWUA AS-SALAMA MAA KUNNAA NAA’MALU MIN SOOIN BALAAA INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThose whom the angels terminate their life while they are unjust unto themselves, then they would offer submission (saying): “We used not to do any evil,” (the angels will reply): “Aye! Verily knoweth God well what ye were doing.\nفَادْخُلُوْۤا اَبْوَابَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ؕ فَلَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(29)\nEZAA AABWAABA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA FALABESA MASWAA AL-MUTAKABBEREENA.\nTherefore enter ye the gates of Hell, to abide in it; Woeful indeed will be the abode of the haughty ones!\nوَقِيْلَ لِلَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا مَاذَاۤ اَنْزَلَ رَبُّكُمْ‌ؕ قَالُوْا خَيْرًاؕ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةٌ‌  ؕ وَلَدَارُ الْاٰخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ ‌ ؕ وَلَنِعْمَ دَارُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(30)\nWA QEELAD LILLAZEENA TAQAW MAA ANZALAL RABBUKUM QAALOO KHAYRAN LIL-LAZEENA AAHSANOOA FEE HAAZEHE DUNYAA HASANATUL WALADAARU AAKHERATE KHAYRUL WALANEA’MA DAARU MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd it is said unto those who guard themselves against evil: “What is that hath sent down your Lord?” Say they: “Good; For those who do good in this world is good; and indeed the abode of the hereafter is better; and excellent indeed is the abode of the pious ones,\nجَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ يَّدْخُلُوْنَهَا تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ‌ لَهُمْ فِيْهَا مَا يَشَآءُوْنَ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَجْزِى اللّٰهُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(31)\nJANNAATU A’ADNIN YYADKHULOONAHAA TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO LAHUM FEEHAA MAA YASHAAOONA KAZAALEKA YAJZEAA LAAHO MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nGardens of eternity, they shall enter therein, beneath them flow rivers; they shall have in them whatever they desire for; Thus doth God reward the pious ones,\nالَّذِيْنَ تَتَوَفّٰٮهُمُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ طَيِّبِيْنَ‌ ۙ يَقُوْلُوْنَ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمُۙ ادْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(32)\nLAZEENA TATAWAFFAAHUMU AL-MALAAEKATU TAYBEENA YAQOOLOONA SALAAMUN A’LAYKOMUL ADKHULOOA JANNATA BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThose whom the angels take away in a good state, (the angels) while receiving them will say: “Peace be on you; Enter ye the Garden, for what ye were doing.\nهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ اَوْ يَاْتِىَ اَمْرُ رَبِّكَ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ فَعَلَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ؕ وَمَا ظَلَمَهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(33)\nHAL YANZOROONA ILLAA AN TAA-TEYAHOMUL AL-MALAAEKATU AW HATTAA AMRUL RABBEKA KAZAALEKA FA-A’LA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WA MAA ZALAMAHUMU LAAHO WA LAAKIL KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nWhat! Await they aught save that come unto them the angels or cometh (to pass) the decree of thy Lord? Thus did those before them; And God was not unjust unto them, but they were unto their own selves unjust.\nفَاَصَابَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا عَمِلُوْا وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(34)\nFAASAABAHUM SAYAAATU MAA A’MELOO WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nSo afflicted them the evils what they did; and encompassed them that which they were scoffing at.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا لَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَا عَبَدْنَا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ شَىْءٍ نَّحْنُ وَلَاۤ اٰبَآؤُنَا وَلَا حَرَّمْنَا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ شَىْءٍ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ فَعَلَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ۚ فَهَلْ عَلَى الرُّسُلِ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(35)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA ASHRAKOO LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA A’ABADNAA MIN DOONEHI MIN SHAY-IN NNAHNU WA LAA AAABAAUNAA WA LAA HARRAMNAA MIN DOONEHI MIN SHAYIN KAZAALEKA FA-A’LA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FA HAL A’LAL AR-RUSULE ILLAA BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nAnd say they who associated (other gods with God) “If God had willed, we had worshipped not aught besides Him, (neither) we nor our fathers; nor had we (forbidden) aught without a (decree from) Him;” Even so did (say) those before them; Is then (aught) incumbent upon (Our) apostles save a clear delivery (plain preaching of the message)?\nوَلَقَدْ بَعَثْنَا فِىْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ رَّسُوْلًا اَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَاجْتَنِبُوا الطَّاغُوْتَ‌ۚ فَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ هَدَى اللّٰهُ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ حَقَّتْ عَلَيْهِ الضَّلٰلَةُ‌ ؕ فَسِيْرُوْا فِىْ الْاَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(36)\nWA LAQAD BAA’ASNAA FEE KULLE UMMATIN RASOOLANY SAALEHAN BODUL LAAHA WAAJTANEBOOA AT-TAAGHOOTA FA-MINHUM MAN LAZEENA LAAHO WA MINHUM MAN HAQQAT A’LAYHE AZ-ZALAALATU FA SEEROO FEE ARZE FANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MOKAZZEBEENAZ.\nAnd indeed raised We in every nation an apostle (of Ours) (preaching) that “Worship ye God (only), and shun ye (the worship of every kind of) idol,” so of them were some whom God guided, and of them were others on whom error was confirmed; Therefore travel ye in the earth, then see what hath been the end of the beliers.\nاِنْ تَحْرِصْ عَلٰى هُدٰٮهُمْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يُّضِلُّ‌ وَمَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(37)\nIN TAHRES A’LAA HODAAHUM WA FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE MAN YYUZELLU WA MAA LAHUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nIf covetest thou for their guidance, yet verily God guideth not those whom He leaveth to stray, and neither for them shall be any of the helpers.\nوَ اَقْسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ جَهْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْ‌ۙ لَا يَبْعَثُ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّمُوْتُ‌ؕ بَلٰى وَعْدًا عَلَيْهِ حَقًّا وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(38)\nWA AAQSAMOOA BIL-LAAHE JAHDA AAYMAANEHEM LAA YABA’ASU LAAHO MAN YYAMOOTU BALAA WA’DAN A’LAYHE HAQQAN WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd swear they by God, with the strongest of their oaths that God will raise not one who dieth; Nay, but it is a promise binding on Him in truth, but most people know it not,\nلِيُبَيِّنَ لَهُمُ الَّذِىْ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ فِيْهِ وَ لِيَعْلَمَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا كٰذِبِيْنَ‏(39)\nLEEBAYNA LAHOMUL LAZEE YAKHTALEFOON FEEHE WA LEEA’LAMA LAZEENA KAFAROO ANNAHUM KAANOO KAAZEBEENA.\n(They will be raised up) so that He might manifest unto them that which they differed about, and (that) those who disbelieved might know that they were liars.\nاِنَّمَا قَوْلُنَا لِشَىْءٍ اِذَاۤ اَرَدْنٰهُ اَنْ نَّقُوْلَ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(40)\nINNAMAA QAWLUNAA LE-SHAY-IN EZAA AARADNAAHU AN NNAQOOLA LAHU KUN FAYAKUN.\nVerily only Our word for a thing when We will it is that We say unto it, ‘Be’ and it exists.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هَاجَرُوْا فِى اللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا ظُلِمُوْا لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً‌  ؕ وَلَاَجْرُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَكْبَرُ‌ۘ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(41)\nWAL LAZEENA HAAJAROO FIL LAAHE MIN BA’DE MAA ZULEMOOA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FIL DUNYAA HASANATANW WALAAJRU AAKHERATE AKBARO LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nAnd those who migrate in (the cause of) God after they are oppressed, certainly We will give them good (recompense) in this world; and certainly the reward in the hereafter is much greater, if they only know (this),\nالَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْا وَعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ‏(42)\nLAZEENA SABAROO WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nThose who endured patiently and on their Lord (only) do they rely.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ اِلَّا رِجَالًا نُّوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْهِمْ‌ فَسْئَلُوْۤا اَهْلَ الذِّكْرِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(43)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA ILLAA REJAALAN NNOOHEAA ELAYHIM FASALOOA AHLAL AZ-ZEKRE IN KUNTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd We sent not before thee but men (as Our apostles), We revealed unto them; So ask ye the people of ‘Dhikr’ (the Qur’an) if ye know not,\nبِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَالزُّبُرِ‌ؕ وَاَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الذِّكْرَ لِتُبَيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ مَا نُزِّلَ اِلَيْهِمْ وَلَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(44)\nBIL-BAYYENAATE WAALZZUBURE WA ANZALNAA ELAYKA KHASEYAR LETUBAYNA LIN-NAASE MAA NUZZELA ELAYHIM WA LA-A’LLAHUM YATAFAKKAROON.\nWith clear proofs (miracles) and scriptures; and We sent down unto thee the ‘Dhikr’ (The Reminder i.e., Qur’an) that thou mayest make clear unto mankind what hath been sent down unto them, that they may reflect\nاَفَاَمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ مَكَرُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ اَنْ يَّخْسِفَ اللّٰهُ بِهِمُ الْاَرْضَ اَوْ يَاْتِيَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(45)\nAAFAAMENA LAZEENA MAKAROOA SAYYE-AATE AN YAKHSEFA LAAHO BEHEMUL ARZA AW YAATEEHUMU A’ZAABO MIN HAYSO LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nWhat! then feel they secure, who plan evil devices, (against) God causing them swallowed up by the earth, or cometh unto them the wrath from whence they perceive not?\nاَوْ يَاْخُذَهُمْ فِىْ تَقَلُّبِهِمْ فَمَا هُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَۙ‏(46)\nAW YAAKHUZAHUM FEE TAQALLUBEHEM FAMAA HUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nOr that He seizeth them during their movement, they shall not frustrate (God's decree),\nاَوْ يَاْخُذَهُمْ عَلٰى تَخَوُّفٍؕ فَاِنَّ رَبَّكُمْ لَرَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(47)\nAW YAAKHUZAHUM A’LAA TAKHAWFIN FA-INNAL TAQUL LA-RAOOFUR RAHEEM.\nOr He seizeth them by a gradual loss, for verily your Lord is Pitiful and All-Merciful.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلٰى مَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ يَّتَفَيَّؤُا ظِلٰلُهٗ عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ وَالشَّمَآئِلِ سُجَّدًا لِّلَّهِ وَهُمْ دٰخِرُوْنَ‏(48)\nAWALAM YARAW ELAA MAA KHALAQAL LAAHO MIN SHAY-IN YYATAFAYUA ZELAALUH A’NIL YAMEENE WAALSSHAMAAELE SUJJADANW LILLAAH WA HUM DAAKHEROONA.\nOr see they not towards what God hath created that everything turneth its shadow to the right and to the left, prostrating in obeisance unto God, while they lie abased.\nوَلِلّٰهِ يَسْجُدُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ وَّالْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(49)\nLILLAAHE YASJUDU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE MIN DAAAB-BATIL WWAALMALAAEKATU WA HUM LAA YASTAKBEROONA.\nAnd prostrateth in obeisance unto God (only) whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth, (and) of the (moving) creatures, and the angels (too), and they pride not.\nيَخَافُوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ مِّنْ فَوْقِهِمْ وَيَفْعَلُوْنَ مَا يُؤْمَرُوْنَ ۩‏(50)\nYAKHAAFOONA RABBAHUM MIN FAWQEHIM WA YAF-A’LOON MAA YUMAROONA.\nThey fear their Lord (Supreme) above them and do what they are commanded.\nوَقَالَ اللّٰهُ لَا تَتَّخِذُوْۤا اِلٰهَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ‌ۚ اِنَّمَا هُوَ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ‌ ۚ فَاِيَّاىَ فَارْهَبُوْنِ‏(51)\nWA QAALA LAAHO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA AELAAHAYNE NAYNE INNAMAA HOWA ELAAHUN WAAHED FA-IYYAA-YA FARHABOON.\nGod hath said: “Take ye not two gods, Verily, Verily, He is only One God; So of Me (alone) should ye be afraid.\nوَلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ وَلَهُ الدِّيْنُ وَاصِبًا‌ ؕ اَفَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(52)\nWA LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA ARZE LAHUL DEENO WAASEBAN AAFAGHAYRA LAAHE TATTAQOON.\nAnd His it is whatever is in the heavens and the earth, and unto Him (only) should obedience constantly be; Do ye then fear (any one else) other than God?\nوَمَا بِكُمْ مِّنْ نِّعْمَةٍ فَمِنَ اللّٰهِ‌ ثُمَّ اِذَا مَسَّكُمُ الضُّرُّ فَاِلَيْهِ تَجْئَرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\nWA MAA BEKUM MIN NEA’MATIN NAASE LAAHE SUMMA EZAA MASSAKUMU AZ-ZURRU FA ELAYHE TAJAROONA.\nWhatever of the bounty is with you, it is from God, then when any distress toucheth you, unto Him do ye cry for help.\nثُمَّ اِذَا كَشَفَ الضُّرَّ عَنْكُمْ اِذَا فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْكُمْ بِرَبِّهِمْ يُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(54)\nSUMMA EZAA KASHAFA AZ-ZURRA A’NKUM EZAA FAREEQUM MINKUM BE-RABBEHIM YUSHREKOON.\nYet when removeth He the distress from you, lo! some of you associate others with their Lord,\nلِيَكْفُرُوْا بِمَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ‌ؕ فَتَمَتَّعُوْا‌ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(55)\nLE-YAKFOROO BEMAA AATAYNAAHUM FATAMATTAO’O FA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON.\nThat they may deny what We have given them; (Say O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “then enjoy your selves (for a time); for soon will ye know.\nوَيَجْعَلُوْنَ لِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ نَصِيْبًا مِّمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ‌ؕ تَاللّٰهِ لَتُسْئَلُنَّ عَمَّا كُنْتُمْ تَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(56)\nWA YAJ-A’LOONA LEMAKH LAA YA’LAMOON NASEEBAN MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM TAALLLAAHE LA-TUS-A-LUNNA A’MMAA KUNTUM TAFTAROONA.\nAnd they assign for what they know not, a portion of what We have provided them with; By God! Certainly ye shall be questioned about what ye have been forging.\nوَيَجْعَلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ الْبَنٰتِ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ۙ وَلَهُمْ مَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَ‏(57)\nWA YAJ-A’LOONA LILLAAHE AL-BANAATE WALADAN WA LAHUM MAA YASHTAHOONA.\nAnd they ascribe daughters to God Glory be to Him; And for themselves (they ascribe sons) what they desire!\nوَاِذَا بُشِّرَ اَحَدُهُمْ بِالْاُنْثٰى ظَلَّ وَجْهُهٗ مُسْوَدًّا وَّهُوَ كَظِيْمٌ‌ۚ‏(58)\nWA EZAA BUSSHERA AHADOHUM BIL-AUNSAA ZALLA WAJHUH MUSWADDAN WA KAZEEMUN.\nAnd when is announced unto (any) one of them a daughter, black becometh his face and he is filled with wrath.\nيَتَوَارٰى مِنَ الْقَوْمِ مِنْ سُوْۤءِ مَا بُشِّرَ بِهٖ ؕ اَيُمْسِكُهٗ عَلٰى هُوْنٍ اَمْ يَدُسُّهٗ فِى التُّرَابِ‌ ؕ اَلَا سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(59)\nYATAWAARAA MENAL QAWMIL MIN SOOE MAA BUSSHERA BEHI AAYUMSEKUH A’LAA HOONIN AM YADUSSUH FIL AT-TURAABE ALAA SAAA-A MAA YAHKUMOONA.\nHe hideth himself from the people, of the evil for the tidings given to him, (he pondereth whether) he shall keep her with disgrace or bury her (alive) in the dust? Behold, (how) evil it is what they decide.\nلِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ مَثَلُ السَّوْءِ‌ۚ وَلِلّٰهِ الْمَثَلُ الْاَعْلٰى‌ ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(60)\nLILLAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE MASALUL SAW LILLAAHE MASALUL A-A’LAA WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nFor those who believe not in the hereafter is an evil similitude, and God’s is the highest similitude; for He is the Mighty, the All-Wise.\nوَلَوْ يُؤَاخِذُ اللّٰهُ النَّاسَ بِظُلْمِهِمْ مَّا تَرَكَ عَلَيْهَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ وَّلٰكِنْ يُّؤَخِّرُهُمْ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى‌‌ۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَجَلُهُمْ لَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَ سَاعَةً‌ وَّلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA LAW YUAAKHEZU LAAHO NAASA BEZULMEHEM MAA TARAKA A’LAYHAA MIN DAAAB-BATIL LAAKIL YYUAKKHERUHUM ELAA ELAA AJALIM FA-EZAA JAAA-A AAJALUHUM LAA YASTAAKHEROONA SAAA’ATAN WA LAA YASTAQDEMOONA.\nIf God had to take to task the people for their inequity, He would not leave on it (the earth) a single moving being but He respiteth them until an appointed term; so when cometh their doom, they shall delay it not (even) an hour, nor shall they bring it on before (its appointed time).\nوَيَجْعَلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ مَا يَكْرَهُوْنَ وَتَصِفُ اَلْسِنَتُهُمُ الْكَذِبَ اَنَّ لَهُمُ الْحُسْنٰى‌ؕ لَا جَرَمَ اَنَّ لَهُمُ النَّارَ وَ اَنَّهُمْ مُّفْرَطُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA YAJ-A’LOONA LILLAAHE MAA YAKRAHOONA WATASEFU AALSENATUHUMU AL-KAZEBA ANNAL LAHOMUL HUSNAA LAA JARAMA ANNAL LAHOMUL NAARAL WA ANNAHUM MMUFRATOONA.\nAnd they assign unto God what they (themselves) hate and attribute their tongues falsely that for them are (all) good things; Inevitably there shall be for them the (Hell) fire and they shall be the foremost to it.\nتَاللّٰهِ لَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمَمٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فَهُوَ وَلِيُّهُمُ الْيَوْمَ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(63)\nTAALLLAAHE LAQAD ARSALNAA ELAA OMAMIN MIN QABLEKA FAZAYNA LAHOMUL SHAYTAANO A-A’MAALAHUM FAHOWA WALEEHUMU YAWMA WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nBy God! indeed sent We (Our) Apostles unto people before thee, but Satan made unto them their deeds fair-seeming, so he is their guardian today, and for them shall be a grievous chastisement.\nوَمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ اِلَّا لِتُبَيِّنَ لَهُمُ الَّذِى اخْتَلَفُوْا فِيْهِ‌ۙ وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(64)\nWA MAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKA KETAABA ILLAA LETUBAYNA LAHOMUL LAZIS TALAFOO FEEHE WA HODANW WA RAHMATAL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nAnd We sent not down unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muham mad!) the Book (the Qur’an) but that thou mayest explain unto them that which they differ about, and (as) a guidance and a mercy for the people who believe.\nوَاللّٰهُ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَحْيَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّسْمَعُوْنَ‏(65)\nWAL LAAHO ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-AHYAA BEHIL ARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA WA INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YASMA-O’ON.\nAnd God hath sent down from the heavens water, then enliveneth He with it the earth after its death; Verily, in this is a sign for people who listen.\nوَاِنَّ لَكُمْ فِىْ الْاَنْعَامِ لَعِبْرَةً‌  ؕ نُّسْقِيْكُمْ مِّمَّا فِىْ بُطُوْنِهٖ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ فَرْثٍ وَّدَمٍ لَّبَنًا خَالِصًا سَآئِغًا لِّلشّٰرِبِيْنَ‏(66)\nWA INNA LAKUM FEE AL-AANA’AAME LAE’EBRATAN NNUSQEEKUM MIMMAA FEE BUTOONEH MIN BAYNE FARSIN WWADAMIN LLABANAN KHAALESAN SAAEGHAN LLELSSHAAREBEENA.\nAnd verily for you there in the cattle is a lesson; We give you to drink what is in their bellies, from betwixt the faeces and the blood, milk pure, easy and palatable for those who drink (it).\nوَمِنْ ثَمَرٰتِ النَّخِيْلِ وَالْاَعْنَابِ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ مِنْهُ سَكَرًا وَّرِزْقًا حَسَنًا ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA MIN SAMARAATE AN-NAKHEELE WAL AAA’NAABE TATTAKHEZOONA MINHO SAKARAN WWAREZQAN HASANAN INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd of the fruits of the date-palms, and the grapes - obtain ye from them (drinks of) intoxication and goodly sustenance; Verily in this is a sign for people who understand.\nوَاَوْحٰى رَبُّكَ اِلَى النَّحْلِ اَنِ اتَّخِذِىْ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوْتًا وَّمِنَ الشَّجَرِ وَمِمَّا يَعْرِشُوْنَۙ‏(68)\nWAAWHAA RABBOKA ELAL AN-NAHLE SAALEHAN ATTAKHEZEAA MENAL JEBAALE BUYOOTAN WWAMENA ASH-SHAJARE WA MIMMAA YAA’RESHOONA.\nAnd revealed thy Lord unto the bee saying: “Make thou hives in the mountains and in the trees and in what they (men) build,\nثُمَّ كُلِىْ مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِ فَاسْلُكِىْ سُبُلَ رَبِّكِ ذُلُلًا‌ ؕ يَخْرُجُ مِنْۢ بُطُوْنِهَا شَرَابٌ مُّخْتَلِفٌ اَلْوَانُهٗ فِيْهِ شِفَآءٌ لِّلنَّاسِ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(69)\nSUMMA KULEAA MIN KULLE SAMARAATE FAASLUKEAA SUBULA RABBEKE ZULULAN YAKHROJO MIN BUTOONEHAA SHARAABUN MMUKHTALEFUN AALWAANUH FEEHE SHEFAAUN LLELNNAASE INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nThen eat thou of all the fruits and walk thou in the ways of thy Lord submissively.” There cometh out from within it a drink of divers colours, in it is healing for men; Verily in this is a sign for the people who reflect.\nوَاللّٰهُ خَلَقَكُمْ ثُمَّ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ‌ۙ وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّرَدُّ اِلٰٓى اَرْذَلِ الْعُمُرِ لِكَىْ لَا يَعْلَمَ بَعْدَ عِلْمٍ شَيْئًا‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌ قَدِيْرٌ‏(70)\nWAL LAAHO KHALAQAKUM SUMMA YATAWAFFAAKUM WA MINKUM MAN YYURADDU ELAA AARZALE AL-U’UMURE LEKAY LAA YAA’LAMA BA’DA I’LMIN SHAYAN INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM QADEER.\nAnd God hath created you, then He taketh you away, and of you is he who is reverted to the lowest state of the age, so that he knoweth not aught after (once) having knowledge: Verily God is All-Knowing, All-Powerful.\nوَاللّٰهُ فَضَّلَ بَعْضَكُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ فِى الرِّزْقِ‌ۚ فَمَا الَّذِيْنَ فُضِّلُوْا بِرَآدِّىْ رِزْقِهِمْ عَلٰى مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُهُمْ فَهُمْ فِيْهِ سَوَآءٌ‌ ؕ اَفَبِنِعْمَةِ اللّٰهِ يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(71)\nWAL LAAHO FAZZALA BAA’ZAKUM A’LAA ELAA FIL AR-REZQE FAMAA LAZEENA FUZZELOOA BERAADDEAA REZQEHEM A’LAA MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOHUM FAHUM FEEHE SAWAAA-UN AAFABENEA’MATE LAAHE YAJHADOON.\nAnd God hath favoured some of you above the others in the provision of sustenance, now those who have been more favoured give not their sustenance to those whom their right hands possess, (the slaves) so that they may be equal therein; What! Is it then the bounty of God they deny?\nوَاللّٰهُ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا وَّ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اَزْوَاجِكُمْ بَنِيْنَ وَحَفَدَةً وَّرَزَقَكُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ‌ؕ اَفَبِالْبَاطِلِ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَبِنِعْمَتِ اللّٰهِ هُمْ يَكْفُرُوْنَۙ‏(72)\nWAL LAAHO JA-A’LA LAKUM MIN ANFOSEKUM AZWAAJANW WA JA-A’LA LAKUM MIN AAZWAAJEKUM BANEENA WAHAFADATAN WWARAZAQAKUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE AFA-BIL-BAATELE YOAMENOONA WABENEA’MATE LAAHE HUM YAKFOROON.\nAnd God hath given you wives of your own selves, and hath given you from your wives sons and grandchildren, and sustained you of good things; What! Is it then in the falsehood they believe, and (a) in the bounty of God (that) they disbelieve?\nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَمْلِكُ لَهُمْ رِزْقًا مِّنَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(73)\nWA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YAMLEKU LAHUM RIZQAN MENAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE SHAY-ANW WA LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA.\nAnd they worship other than God that which owneth not for them any sustenance (aught) from the heavens and the earth, nor have they (whom they worship) any power?\nفَلَا تَضْرِبُوْا لِلّٰهِ الْاَمْثَالَ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(74)\nFALAA TAZREBOOA LILLAAHE AL-AAMSAALA INNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO WA ANTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nSo coin ye not any similitudes to God; Verily God knoweth (everything) and ye know not.\nضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا عَبْدًا مَّمْلُوْكًا لَّا يَقْدِرُ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ وَّمَنْ رَّزَقْنٰهُ مِنَّا رِزْقًا حَسَنًا فَهُوَ يُنْفِقُ مِنْهُ سِرًّا وَّجَهْرًا‌ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوٗنَ‌ؕ اَ لْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(75)\nZARABA LAAHO MASALAA A’BDAN MMAMLOOKAN LAA YAQDERU A’LAA SHAY-IN WWAMAN RRAZAQNAAHU MINNAA RIZQAN HASANAN FAHOWA YUNFEQO MINHO SIRRAN WWAJAHRAN HAL YASTAWNA A’ZAABAN LHAMDU LIL-LAAH BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSetteth forth God the similitude (of two men: one) a slave, a property of another, who hath no power over aught, and (the one) whom We sustained from unto Ourselves a goodly sustenance, and he spendeth from it secretly and openly; Are the two equal? All praise is God’s! But most of them know it not.\nوَضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلاً رَّجُلَيْنِ اَحَدُهُمَاۤ اَبْكَمُ لَا يَقْدِرُ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ وَّهُوَ كَلٌّ عَلٰى مَوْلٰٮهُۙ اَيْنَمَا يُوَجِّههُّ لَا يَاْتِ بِخَيْرٍ‌ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوِىْ هُوَۙ وَمَنْ يَّاْمُرُ بِالْعَدْلِ‌ۙ وَهُوَ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(76)\nWA ZARABA LAAHO MASALAAN RRAJULAYNE AAHADUHUMAA AABKAMU LAA YAQDERU A’LAA SHAY-IN WA KALLUN A’LAA MAWLAAHU AYNAMAA YOOJJEHHHU LAA TAKOONOO BEKHAYRIN HAL YASTAWEE HOWA WA MAN YYAAMURU BIL-A’DL WA HOWA A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nSetteth forth God the similitude of two men; one of them is dumb, unable to do anything, he is a burden to his master; wherever he (the master) sendeth him, he bringeth no good; can he be equal to him who enjoineth justice and he (himself) is on the straight path?\nوَلِلّٰهِ غَيْبُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَمَاۤ اَمْرُ السَّاعَةِ اِلَّا كَلَمْحِ الْبَصَرِ اَوْ هُوَ اَقْرَبُ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(77)\nLILLAAHE GHAYBU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA MAA AMRUL AS-SAAA’ATE ILLAA KALAMHE AL-BASARE AW HOWA AAQRABU INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nAnd God’s is the unseen (worlds) of the heavens and the earth; and the matter of the Hour (of Judgment) is but like a twinkling of the eye, or nigher still; Verily God over all things hath power.\nوَاللّٰهُ اَخْرَجَكُمْ مِّنْۢ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ شَيْئًا ۙ وَّ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصٰرَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ‌ ۙ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(78)\nWAL LAAHO AAKHRAJAKUM MIN BUTOONE MINHUNNA LAA TA’LAMOON SHAY-ANW WA JA-A’LA LAKOMUL JA-A’LA WAL AABSAARA WA ABSAARA WAL LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nAnd God hath brought you forth from the wombs of your mothers - ye knew not anything, and He gave you hearing and the sight and the hearts, that ye may give thanks.\nاَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلَى الطَّيْرِ مُسَخَّرٰتٍ فِىْ جَوِّ السَّمَآءِ ؕ مَا يُمْسِكُهُنَّ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(79)\nALAM YARAW ELAL TAYRE MUSAKKHARAATIN FEE JAW SAMAAA-E MAA YUMSEKOHUNNA ILLAA LAAH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nWhat! See they not towards the birds held poised in the air in the sky? Nothing holdeth them but God; Verily in this are signs for a people who believe\nوَاللّٰهُ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْۢ بُيُوْتِكُمْ سَكَنًا وَّجَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ جُلُوْدِ الْاَنْعَامِ بُيُوْتًا تَسْتَخِفُّوْنَهَا يَوْمَ ظَعْنِكُمْ وَيَوْمَ اِقَامَتِكُمْ‌ۙ وَمِنْ اَصْوَافِهَا وَاَوْبَارِهَا وَاَشْعَارِهَاۤ اَثَاثًا وَّمَتَاعًا اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(80)\nWAL LAAHO JA-A’LA LAKUM MIN BUYOOTEKUM SAKANAN ANHAARAWN LAKUM MIN JULOODE AL-AANA’AAME BUYOOTAN TASTAKHEFFOONAHAA YAWMA ZAA’NEKUM WA YAWMA AEQAAMATEKUM WA MIN AASWAAFEHAA WAAWBAAREHAA WAASHA’AAREHAA AASAASAN WA MATAA-A’L ELAA HEEN.\nAnd God hath made for you of your houses, a place of rest (and the quiet) and hath made for you of the skins of the cattle houses which ye find so light to carry on the day of your march and on the day of your camping, and of their wool and their fur and their hair (he hath provided for you) (useful) goods of convenience and a provision for a time.\nوَاللّٰهُ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّمَّا خَلَقَ ظِلٰلًا وَّجَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الْجِبَالِ اَكْنَانًا وَّجَعَلَ لَكُمْ سَرَابِيْلَ تَقِيْكُمُ الْحَرَّ وَسَرَابِيْلَ تَقِيْكُمْ بَاْسَكُمْ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُتِمُّ نِعْمَتَهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(81)\nWAL LAAHO JA-A’LA LAKUM MIMMAA KHALAQAL ZELAALAN ANHAARAWN LAKUM MENAL JEBAALE AAKNAANAN ANHAARAWN LAKUM SARAABEELA TAQEEKUMU AL-HARRA WASARAABEELA TAQEEKUM BAASAKUM KAZAALEKA YUTEMMU NE’MATAHU A’LAYKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TUSLEMOONA.\nAnd God hath made for you, of what He hath created shelters, and hath made for you (some) of the mountains (as) places of refuge, and He hath made for you garments to guard you against the heat (and cold), and the garments to protect you in your fighting; Thus completed! He, His bounties on you so that ye may submit (unto Him thankfully).\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(82)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FA-INNAMAA A’LAYKA BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nBut if turn they away, then on thee is incumbent only the clear delivery (of Our message).\nيَعْرِفُوْنَ نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ يُنْكِرُوْنَهَا وَاَكْثَرُهُمُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(83)\nYA’REFOONA NEA’MATAL LAAHE SUMMA YUNKEROONAHAA WAAKSARUHUMU KAAFEROON.\nThey recognise the bounties of God, and yet they deny them, and most of them are infidels\nوَيَوْمَ نَبْعَثُ مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ شَهِيْدًا ثُمَّ لَا يُؤْذَنُ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَلَا هُمْ يُسْتَعْتَبُوْنَ‏(84)\nWA YAWMA NABA’ASU MIN KULLE UMMATIN SHAHEEDAA SUMMA LAA YUZANU LILLAZEENA KAFAROO WA LAA HUM HUM YUSTA’TABOON.\nAnd on the day We will raise up from among every people a witness, then shall be no permission for those who disbelieve (to make any excuses) nor shall they be allowed to solicit any amends.\nوَاِذَا رَاَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوا الْعَذَابَ فَلَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA EZAA RA-AL LAZEENA ZALAMOOA A’ZAABA FALAA YOKHAFFAFO A’NHUM WA LAA HUM HUM YUNZAROON.\nAnd when those who act unjustly shall see the torment, it shall not be lightened for them, nor shall they be respited.\nوَ اِذَا رَاَ الَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا شُرَكَآءَهُمْ قَالُوْا رَبَّنَا هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ شُرَكَآؤُنَا الَّذِيْنَ كُنَّا نَدْعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِكَ‌ۚ فَاَلْقَوْا اِلَيْهِمُ الْقَوْلَ اِنَّكُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(86)\nWA EZAA RA-AL LAZEENA ASHRAKOO SHURAKAAAHUM QAALOO RABBANAA HAAOOLAAA-E SHURAKAAUNAA LAZEENA KUNNAA NADU’OOA MIN DOONEKA FAALQAWA ELAYHEMUS QAWLA INNAKUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nAnd when those who associate (others with God) will see their associates, they shall say: “O’ Our Lord! These are our associates whom we called besides Thee!” But they will throw (back) unto them (their) word, (and say) “Verily ye are liars!\nوَاَلْقَوْا اِلَى اللّٰهِ يَوْمَئِذٍ ۨالسَّلَمَ‌ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(87)\nWAALQAWA ELAL LAAHE YAWMA-EZIN AS-SALAMA WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nAnd they shall tender submission unto God on that day; And shall depart from them (leaving them in lurch) what they were forging.\nاَ لَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ زِدْنٰهُمْ عَذَابًا فَوْقَ الْعَذَابِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يُفْسِدُوْنَ‏(88)\nA’ZAABAN LLAZEENA KAFAROO WASADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE ZEDNAAHUM A’ZAABAN FAWQA A’ZAABE BEMAA KAANOO YUFSEDOONA.\n(For) those who disbelieved and hinder people from the way of God: And We unto them will increase torment over torment for they were making mischief.\nوَيَوْمَ نَبْعَثُ فِىْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ شَهِيْدًا عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِهِمْ‌ وَجِئْنَا بِكَ شَهِيْدًا عَلٰى هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ‌ؕ وَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ تِبْيَانًا لِّكُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّ هُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً وَّبُشْرٰى لِلْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(89)\nWA YAWMA NABA’ASU FEE KULLE UMMATIN SHAHEEDAA A’LAYHIM MIN ANFOSEHIM WAJENAA BEKA SHAHEEDAA A’LAA HAAOOLAAA-E WA NAZZALNAA A’LAYKA KETAABA TEBYAANAN LEKULLE SHAY-IN WA HODAM WA RAHMATAL WA BUSHRAA LIL-MUSLEMEENA.\nAnd on the day when We will raise up in every people from among themselves, a witness (upon them) and bring thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) as a witness upon (all) these; and We have sent down upon thee the Book (The Qur’an) explaining everything, and a guidance, and mercy, and glad tidings unto those who submit themselves (To God).\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَاْمُرُ بِالْعَدْلِ وَالْاِحْسَانِ وَاِيْتَآىئِ ذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَيَنْهٰى عَنِ الْفَحْشَآءِ وَالْمُنْكَرِ وَالْبَغْىِ‌ۚ يَعِظُكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(90)\nINNAL LAAHA YAAMURU BIL-A’DL WA EHSAANE WAAYTAAAAE ZIL QURBAA WAYANHAA A’NIL FAHSHAAA-E WAL MUNKARE WAL BAGHAAE YA-E’ZOKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nVerily, God enjoineth justice and benevolence (to others) and giving unto the kindred, and forbiddeth lewdness, and evil, and rebellion; He exhorteth you that ye may take heed.\nوَ اَوْفُوْا بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ اِذَا عَاهَدتُّمْ وَلَا تَنْقُضُوا الْاَيْمَانَ بَعْدَ تَوْكِيْدِهَا وَقَدْ جَعَلْتُمُ اللّٰهَ عَلَيْكُمْ كَفِيْلًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(91)\nWA AAWFOOA BEA’AHDE LAAHE EZAA A’AAHADTTUM WA LAA TANQUZOOA AL-AAYMAANA BA’DA TAWKEEDEHAA WA QAD JAA’ALTUMU LAAHA A’LAYKUM KAFEELAN INNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA TAF-A’LOON.\nAnd fulfil ye the covenant of God when ye have covenanted, and break ye not the oaths after ratification thereof while indeed ye have appointed God over you a surety (for it); Verily God knoweth (everything) what ye do.\nوَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا كَالَّتِىْ نَقَضَتْ غَزْلَهَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ قُوَّةٍ اَنْكَاثًا ؕ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ اَيْمَانَكُمْ دَخَلًاۢ بَيْنَكُمْ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ اُمَّةٌ هِىَ اَرْبٰى مِنْ اُمَّةٍ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا يَبْلُوْكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِهٖ ‌ؕ وَلَيُبَيِّنَنَّ لَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(92)\nWA LAA TAKOONOO KA-LATEE NAQAZAT GHAZLAHAA MIN BA’DE QUWWATIN AANKAASAN TATTAKHEZOONA AAYMAANAKUM DAKHALAN BAYNAKUM AN TAKOONA UMMATUN HEYA AARBAA MIN UMMATIN INNAMAA YABLOOKUMU LAAHO BEHI WALAYUBAYNANNA LAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE MAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOONA.\nAnd be not like unto her who unraveleth her yarn, dis joining it into thin filaments, after she hath made it spun strong, ye take your oaths as means of deceit between you for one nation is more flourishing than (other) nation. Verily God only trieth you by this; And most assuredly He will make it clear unto you on the Day of Judgment about what ye were differing.\nوَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَجَعَلَكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلٰكِنْ يُّضِلُّ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ ؕ وَلَتُسْئَلُنَّ عَمَّا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(93)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAJAA’ALAKUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN LAAKIL YYUZELLU MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O WA LA-TUS-A-LUNNA A’MMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd if God willeth He would surely make you all a single nation, but He leaveth to err whomsoever He willeth and guideth whomsoever He willeth; And certainly will ye be question ed of what ye were doing.\nوَلَا تَتَّخِذُوْۤا اَيْمَانَكُمْ دَخَلًاۢ بَيْنَكُمْ فَتَزِلَّ قَدَمٌۢ بَعْدَ ثُبُوْتِهَا وَتَذُوْقُوا السُّوْۤءَ بِمَا صَدَدْتُّمْ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ‌ۚ وَ لَكُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(94)\nWA LAA TATTAKHEZOOA AAYMAANAKUM DAKHALAN BAYNAKUM FATAZELLA QADAMUN BA’DA SUBOOTEHAA WATAZOOQOOA AS-SOOA BEMAA SADADTTUM A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAKUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nAnd take ye not your oaths a means of deceit between you, lest slippeth a foot after it hath been firmly fixed, and ye taste the evil for ye hindered (others) from God’s way; and for you be a great torment.\nوَلَا تَشْتَرُوْا بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ هُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(95)\nWA LAA TASHTAROO BEA’AHDE LAAHE SAMANAN QALEELAA INNAMAA I’NDAL LAAHE HOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nSell ye not the covenant of God for a mean price; for verily with God is that which is better for you, if ye only knew.\nمَا عِنْدَكُمْ يَنْفَدُ‌ وَمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ بَاقٍؕ وَلَنَجْزِيَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْۤا اَجْرَهُمْ بِاَحْسَنِ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(96)\nMAA E’ENDAKUM YANFADU WA MAA I’NDAL LAAHE BAAQIN WALANAJZEENNA LAZEENA SABAROO AJRAHUM BE-AHSANE MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWhat (ever) is with you passeth away and what is with God is everlasting; and certainly We will give those who exercise patience, their return, with the best of what they were doing.\nمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا مِّنْ ذَكَرٍ اَوْ اُنْثٰى وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَلَنُحْيِيَنَّهٗ حَيٰوةً طَيِّبَةً‌ ۚ وَلَنَجْزِيَنَّهُمْ اَجْرَهُمْ بِاَحْسَنِ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(97)\nMAN A’MELA SAALEHAN MIN ZAKARIN AW UNSAA WA HOWA MUMENUN FALANUHYEENNAH HAYWTAN TAYBATAN WA LANAJZEYANNAHUM AJRAHUM BE-AHSANE MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWhosoever did good, whether male or female, and he be a believer, then We will certainly make him live a life good and pure, and certainly We will give them their return with the best of what they were doing.\nفَاِذَا قَرَاْتَ الْقُرْاٰنَ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللّٰهِ مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ الرَّجِيْمِ‏(98)\nFA-EZAA QARAATA QURAANA FAS-TA-I’Z BIL-LAAHE MENAL SHAYTAANE AR-RAJEEME.\nAnd when recitest thou the Qur’an seek thou refuge with God from Satan the accursed.\nاِنَّهٗ لَيْسَ لَهٗ سُلْطٰنٌ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ‏(99)\nINNAHU LAYSA LAHU SULTAANUN A’LAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nVerily there is no authority for him over those who believe and rely on their Lord.\nاِنَّمَا سُلْطٰنُهٗ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَتَوَلَّوْنَهٗ وَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِهٖ مُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(100)\nINNAMAA SULTAANUH A’LAL LAZEENA YATAWALLAWNAH WAL LAZEENA HUM BEHI MUSHREKOONA.\nVerily, his authority is only over those who befriend him and those who associate others with Him.\nوَاِذَا بَدَّلْنَاۤ اٰيَةً مَّكَانَ اٰيَةٍ‌ۙ وَّ اللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يُنَزِّلُ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُفْتَرٍؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(101)\nWA EZAA BAD-DALNAA AAYATAL MMAKAANA AAYATIM WA LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YUNAZZELU QAALOO INNAMAA ANTA MUFTARIN BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd when change We one sign for another sign, and God knoweth best what He sendeth down, say they; “Thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) art only a forger.” Nay! most of them know not.\nقُلْ نَزَّلَهٗ رُوْحُ الْقُدُسِ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ بِالْحَقِّ لِيُثَبِّتَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَهُدًى وَّبُشْرٰى لِلْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(102)\nQUL NAZZALAHU ROOHU AL-QUDUSE MIN RABBEKA BIL-HAQQE LEESABBETA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA HODANW WA BUSHRAA LIL-MUSLEMEENA.\nSay thou (unto the disbelievers O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “The Holy Spirit (Angel Gabriel) hath brought it down (unto thee) from thy Lord with the truth, that it may establish those who believe and as a guidance and glad tidings unto those who submit (themselves to God).\nوَلَقَدْ نَعْلَمُ اَنَّهُمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِنَّمَا يُعَلِّمُهٗ بَشَرٌ‌ؕ لِسَانُ الَّذِىْ يُلْحِدُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ اَعْجَمِىٌّ وَّهٰذَا لِسَانٌ عَرَبِىٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(103)\nWA LAQAD NA’LAMO ANNAHUM YAQOOLOONA INNAMAA YUA’ALLEMUH BASHARUN LESAANU LAZEE YULHEDOONA ELAYHE AAA’JAMEAAAUN WWAHAAZAA LESAANUN A’ARABEAAAUN MOBEEN.\nAnd indeed know We that they say: “It is only a man (that) teacheth him.” The tongue of him whom they (falsely) hint at is outlandish while this language is Arabic (pure and) plain.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِۙ لَا يَهْدِيْهِمُ اللّٰهُ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(104)\nINNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE LAA YAHDEEHEMU LAAHO WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nVerily those who believe not in the signs of God, God guideth them not, and for them shall be a painful torment.\nاِنَّمَا يَفْتَرِى الْكَذِبَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ‌ۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(105)\nINNAMAA YAFTAREAA AL-KAZEBA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL AL-KAAZEBOONA.\nVerily forge the lie only they who believe not in the signs of God, and these, they are the liars.\nمَنْ كَفَرَ بِاللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اِيْمَانِهٖۤ اِلَّا مَنْ اُكْرِهَ وَقَلْبُهٗ مُطْمَئِنٌّۢ بِالْاِيْمَانِ وَلٰكِنْ مَّنْ شَرَحَ بِالْكُفْرِ صَدْرًا فَعَلَيْهِمْ غَضَبٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ‌ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(106)\nMAN KAFARA BIL-LAAHE MIN BA’DE AEEMAANEH ILLAA MAN AUKREHA WAQALBUH MUTMAENNUN BIL-EEMAANE WA LAAKIL MAN SHARAHA BIL-KUFRE SADRAN FA A’LAYHIM GHAZABUN MENAL LAAHE WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nHe who disbelieveth in God after his belief in Him, save he who is compelled while his heart remaineth steadfast with the faith, but he who openeth (his) breast for infidelity, on these is the wrath of God; for them shall be a great torment.\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمُ اسْتَحَبُّوا الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا عَلَى الْاٰخِرَةِ ۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(107)\nZAA LEKA BEAANNAHUMU ASTAHABBOOA HAYAATAD DUNYAA A’LAL AAKHERATE WA ANNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ KAAFEREEN.\nThis because they love the life of this world preferring it over the hereafter, and that God guideth not the infidel people.\nاُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ طَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ وَسَمْعِهِمْ وَاَبْصَارِهِمْ‌ۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْغٰفِلُوْنَ‏(108)\nAOOLAAEKA LAZEENA TABAA’A LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM WASAME’EHEM WA ABSAAREHIM WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL AL-GHAAFELOONA.\nThese are those who, God hath set a seal on their hearts, and (on) their hearing (ears) and (on) their sights (eyes), and these, they are the heedless (ones)\nلَا جَرَمَ اَنَّهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(109)\nLAA JARAMA ANNAHUM FIL AAKHERATE HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nDoubtless (it is) that they in the hereafter, they will be the losers.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لِلَّذِيْنَ هَاجَرُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا فُتِنُوْا ثُمَّ جٰهَدُوْا وَصَبَرُوْۤا ۙ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهَا لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(110)\nSUMMA INNAL RABBAKA LILLAZEENA HAAJAROO MIN BA’DE MAA FUTENOOA SUMMA JAAHADOOA WA SABAROO INNAL RABBAKA MIN BAA’DEHAA LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nThen verily thy Lord unto those who migrate after they are persecuted, then they struggle hard (fight) (for God’s cause) and exercised patience; verily, thy Lord, after that is Oft- Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nيَوْمَ تَاْتِىْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ تُجَادِلُ عَنْ نَّفْسِهَا وَتُوَفّٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا عَمِلَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(111)\nYAWMA TAATEAA KULLO NAFSIM TUJAADELU A’N NNAFSEHAA WA TOWAFFAA KULLO NAFSIM MAA A’MELAT WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\n(Remember) the day when every soul shall come, pleading for itself, and every soul shall be recompensed fully for what (all) it hath done, and they will not be dealt with unjustly.\nوَضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا قَرْيَةً كَانَتْ اٰمِنَةً مُّطْمَئِنَّةً يَّاْتِيْهَا رِزْقُهَا رَغَدًا مِّنْ كُلِّ مَكَانٍ فَكَفَرَتْ بِاَنْعُمِ اللّٰهِ فَاَذَاقَهَا اللّٰهُ لِبَاسَ الْجُوْعِ وَالْخَوْفِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(112)\nWA ZARABA LAAHO MASALAA QARYATAN KAANAT AAAMENATAN MMUTMAENNATAN YYAATEEHAA REZQUHAA RAGHADAN MIN KULLE MAKAANIN FAKAFARAT BEAANU’UME LAAHE FAAZAAQAHAA LAAHO LEBAASA AL-JOOE’E WA KHAWFE BEMAA KAANOO YASNAU’OONA.\nAnd setteth forth God a similitude: “(Like) a town safe and secure, cometh unto it its sustenance in abundance from every side, then it turned ungrateful to the bounties of God, therefore God made it taste of (getting enveloped into) the extreme of hunger and dread for what they were doing.\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَخَذَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ وَهُمْ ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(113)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM RASOOLUM MINHUM FA-KAZZABOOHO TOOFAANO A’ZAABO WA HUM ZAALEMOON.\nAnd indeed did come unto them (Our) Apostle from among themselves, but they belied him, so seized them a torment while they were unjust.\nفَكُلُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ حَلٰلًا طَيِّبًا وَّاشْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ اِيَّاهُ تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(114)\nFA-KOLOO MIMMAA RAZAQAKOMUL LAAHO HALAALAN TAYYEBAA WWAASHKUROOA NEA’MATAL LAAHE IN KUNTUM IYYAAHO TA’BODOONA.\nSo eat ye of what God hath provided you lawful and good (things), and give ye thanks for God’s bounty if unto Him ye worship.\nاِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَيْتَةَ وَ الدَّمَ وَلَحْمَ الْخِنْزِيْرِ وَمَاۤ اُهِلَّ لِغَيْرِ اللّٰهِ بِهٖ‌ۚ فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ غَيْرَ بَاغٍ وَّلَا عَادٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(115)\nINNAMAA HARRAMA A’LAYKOMUL MAYTATA WA AD-DAMA WA LAHMAL KHINZEERE WA MAA OHILLA LE-GHAYRIL LAAHE BEHI FAMANE’ TURRA GHAYRA BAAGHINW WA LAA A’ADIN FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nVerily He hath forbidden unto you what dieth of itself and blood and the flesh of swine and that over which hath been invoked any name other than God’s; but whosoever be forced to the necessity, nor desiring nor (wilfully) transgressing the limit, then verily God is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nوَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا لِمَا تَصِفُ اَلْسِنَتُكُمُ الْكَذِبَ هٰذَا حَلٰلٌ وَّهٰذَا حَرَامٌ لِّتَفْتَرُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ‌ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ لَا يُفْلِحُوْنَؕ‏(116)\nWA LAA TAQOOLOO LEMAKH TASEFU AALSENATUKUMU AL-KAZEBA HAAZAA HALAALUN WWAHAAZAA HARAAMUN LLETAFTAROOA A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA INNAL LAZEENA YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA LAA YUFLEHOONA.\nAnd utter ye not whatever lie describe your tongues (saying): “This is lawful and this is for bidden,” to forge a lie against God; Verily, those who forge a lie against God succeed not.\nمَتَاعٌ قَلِيْلٌ وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(117)\nLIL-MOTAALLAQAATE QALEELUN WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nIt is a very little means of enjoyment and for them is a painful torment.\nوَعَلَى الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا حَرَّمْنَا مَا قَصَصْنَا عَلَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ‌ۚ وَمَا ظَلَمْنٰهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(118)\nWA LAZEENA HAADOO HARRAMNAA MAA QASASNAA A’LAYKA MIN QABLO WA MAA ZALAMNAAHUM WA LAAKIL KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nAnd unto those who were Jews We had forbidden what We have (already) related unto thee from before; And We did them not any injustice, but they were unto their own selves unjust.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لِلَّذِيْنَ عَمِلُوا السُّوْۤءَ بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ تَابُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ وَاَصْلَحُوْۤا ۙ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهَا لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(119)\nSUMMA INNAL RABBAKA LILLAZEENA A’MELUS AS-SOOA BEJAHAALATIN SUMMA TAABOO MIN BA’DE ZAA LEKA WA ASLAHOO INNAL RABBAKA MIN BAA’DEHAA LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nYet verily thy Lord, unto those who do an evil (deed) in ignorance, and turn (repent) after that and make amends, Verily thy Lord is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nاِنَّ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ كَانَ اُمَّةً قَانِتًا لِّلَّهِ حَنِيْفًاؕ وَلَمْ يَكُ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَۙ‏(120)\nINNAL IBRAAHEEMA KAANA UMMATAM QAANETAN LILLAAH HANEEFAN WA LAM YAKU MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nVerily Abraham was an Imam (leader in religion) (for the) people, devoutly obedient to God, upright, and he was not of the polytheists,\nشَاكِرًا لِّاَنْعُمِهِ‌ؕ اِجْتَبٰٮهُ وَهَدٰٮهُ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(121)\nSHAAKERAWN LEAANU’UMEHE AEJTABAAHU WAHADAAHU ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nGrateful for His bounties; He (God) chose him and He guided him on the right path.\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُ فِى الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً‌  ؕ وَاِنَّهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ لَمِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَؕ‏(122)\nWA AATAYNAAHO FIL DUNYAA HASANATANW WA INNAHU FIL AAKHERATE LAMENAS AS-SAALEHEENA.\nAnd We gave him good in this world, and verily he in the hereafter will surely be of the righteous ones.\nثُمَّ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ اَنِ اتَّبِعْ مِلَّةَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ حَنِيْفًا‌ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(123)\nSUMMA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA SAALEHAN ATTABEA’ MILLATA IBRAAHEEMA HANEEFAA WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSo We revealed unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) that thou followeth the religion of Abraham, the upright one; and he was not of the polytheists.\nاِنَّمَا جُعِلَ السَّبْتُ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اخْتَلَفُوْا فِيْهِ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَيَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(124)\nINNAMAA JUE’ELA AS-SABTU A’LAL LAZEENA TALAFOO FEEH WA INNA RABBAKA LAYAHKUMU BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nVerily the sabbath was ordain ed only for those who differed about it; and verily thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Judgment in what they used to differ about.\nاُدْعُ اِلٰى سَبِيْلِ رَبِّكَ بِالْحِكْمَةِ وَالْمَوْعِظَةِ الْحَسَنَةِ‌ وَجَادِلْهُمْ بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ ضَلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ‌ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(125)\nAUDU’U ELAA SABEELIL RABBEKA BIL-HEKMATE WAL MAWE’EZATE HASANATE WAJAADELHUM BIL-LATEE HEYA AAHSANU INNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAN ZALLA A’N SABEELEH WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BILMOHTADEEN.\nAnd call thou unto the way of thy Lord with wisdom and kindly exhortation and dispute with them in the manner which is the best; Verily thy Lord knoweth better of him who hath gone astray from His path; and He knoweth best of those guided aright.\nوَاِنْ عَاقَبْتُمْ فَعَاقِبُوْا بِمِثْلِ مَا عُوْقِبْتُمْ بِهٖ‌ۚ وَلَئِنْ صَبَرْتُمْ لَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لِّلصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(126)\nWA A’AAQABTUM FAA’AAQEBOOA BE-MISLE MAA U’OOQEBTUM BEHI WA LAIN SABARTUM LAHOWAL KHAYRUL LLELSSAABEREENA.\nAnd if ye punish then punish ye as ye were afflicted; But if ye be patient, certainly it will be best for the patient ones.\nوَاصْبِرْ وَمَا صَبْرُكَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ‌ وَلَا تَحْزَنْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا تَكُ فِىْ ضَيْقٍ مِّمَّا يَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(127)\nWAS BIR WA MAA SABRUKA ILLAA BIL-LAAHE WA LAA TAHZAN A’LAYHIM WA LAA TAKU FEE ZAYQIM MIMMAA YAMKOROON.\nAnd be thou patient (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) and thy patience is not but by (the help of) God, and grieve not for them; and distress not thyself at what they devise.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا وَّالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ مُّحْسِنُوْنَ‏(128)\nINNAL LAAHA LAAHA LAZEENA TAQAW WWAALLAZEENA HUM MMUHSENOONA.\nVerily God is with those who guard (themselves against evil), and those who do good (to others).",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and has 128 ayaat. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is recorded from the Holy Prophet (S) that whoever recites this Surah will not be questioned, on the Day of Judgement, about the blessings he received on the Earth and will get the reward equal to the amount of people who left a good will when they died.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites Surah an-Nahl once every month, he will be safe from 70 types of diseases and will be from among the people of Jannah. This Surah should, however, under no circumstance be written and kept in the house or garden as it may have harmful effects. Imam Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if kept in a house or garden, it will soon be destroyed. Indeed this is a weapon that one is only allowed to use against an evil person who is the enemy of Islam."
}
